docs {
  A linkset for a Global Model Number (AI 8013), so GS1's resolver test suite
  can be run against a key that uses a check character pair instead of a
  MOD-10 check digit.

  WHY THIS RECORD EXISTS

  The resolver advertises twenty primary keys in
  /.well-known/gs1resolver, but the suite can only exercise the linkset,
  default-link and redirect tests where a linkset actually exists. Until this
  record is created, the GMN support is verified only at the validator level
  (a wrong pair is refused with 400, a right one reaches 404) and not through
  the suite. Same reasoning for put-partyrole-gln-linkset.

  THE VALUE

  9521890340331TSHIRTP3 is 952… demo range per the module convention, and the
  trailing "P3" is its check character pair, computed with MOD 1021-37 over
  CSET 82 as specified for AI 8013 — not a MOD-10 check digit like every other
  key. Verified two ways: against GS1's reference vectors for
  gs1_lint_csumalpha, and live (…P3 resolves, …P4 is refused with 400).

  Do not "correct" the tail. Changing any character in the model reference
  changes the pair, and the resolver will refuse the value outright.

  AFTER CREATING IT

  Run https://ref.gs1.org/test-suites/resolver/ against
  {{dl-url}}/8013/9521890340331TSHIRTP3 — expected 60/60 as for the GTIN.
}
